{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars","id":966918,"title":"Mental Stability of newly Exalted Solars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-10T14:19:26-07:00","id":966918,"title":"Mental Stability of newly Exalted Solars?","content":"Something I have been wondering about for a long time is just how freshly-Exalted Solars deal with the memories inherited with their exaltation. <br /> <br /> From what I understand, part of the package of Exaltation is that you also receive some memories from your &quot;past lives&quot;. This is how you can justify starting out with several Charms right out of chargen, but what about the actual RP-ing aspect of this? Does it just never come up in your games?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, everyone would handle things a little bit differently, but most likely the most common &quot;last memory&quot; of newly Exalted Solars is that of being hunted down and executed. No near-death experiences, narrow escapes, saves or such.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, you <u>died</u>. Violently. Via people you probably trusted.<br /> <br /> How would that actually cause the character to react. From what I have seen in the books, it never comes up at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:39:32-07:00","id":966927,"title":"","content":"Not exactly I mean the cleaning process on an Exaltation does exist and it could just as easily start at the end due to the tendency for the chosen to die horrible deaths usually at the hands of horrific nightmares. <br /> <br /> Also in 2nd the games assumption in the book was that your character had been an exalt for at least a year, so those things would have been mostly coped with at that time. 3E the explanation for the charms is more that they are outgrowths of one's own abilities partially to make it easier to explain their development and probably to help with the scaling back on the emphasis past lives had in 2nd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:05:00-07:00","id":966939,"title":"","content":"In 1E and 2E, Solars and Lunars can have anywhere from no past life memories, to very vivid ones spanning millennia of time. The default mechanically, for chargen, is remembering only snippets. Sidereals also can potentially remember past lives but, mechanically in 1E-2E, are not allowed to. Or something, I didn't understand that part.<br /> <br /> Green Sun Princes didn't get any memories removed from their exaltations, so they're much more likely to have intense memories, including their Solar past lives' violent deaths at the Usurpation. And voices in their heads. And occasionally being possessed by insane personality echoes that aren't even ghosts, let alone real people, but can still ruin their day.<br /> <br /> However, if a Celestial only lives less than 100 years before they die, they don't tend to leave any memories for their next incarnation. Some of the Usurpation victims were probably young (and quite sane), so there are probably some Solars and Infernals whose most recent past life memories are from a century or even longer before the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> I do think that past life memories are interesting and I hope they aren't <b><i>gone</i></b> for 3E. Does the character consider those memories, and that previous incarnation, to be <i><b>them</b></i> personally, or things that happened to another person from whom they only inherited a legacy? What do they believe about reincarnation, and the continuity of identity and selfhood? How much do they even know about Celestial reincarnation? It's something that ought to come up in RP at some point, unless the character truly has no memories at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-10-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:39:33-07:00","id":966957,"title":"","content":"They're generally fuzzy enough to not cause any real problems. A solar might somehow just <i>know</i> how to find a hidden manse or some secret cache of weapons. They might dream of lost glories and epic wars, or they might see someone and get the unshakeable sense that they know them from somewhere.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it's meant to be source of plot hooks rather than any real drama. There's already plenty of that in Creation as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:51:59-07:00","id":966964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=966939#post966939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the character consider those memories, and that previous incarnation, to be <i><b>them</b></i> personally, or things that happened to another person from whom they only inherited a legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that with low Integrity, a young Solar might not even realize they have memories and information now that they didn't before. It'd take them time to realize they could remember people they'd never met before, living a life very different to their current one, and having information they never learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:58:53-07:00","id":966967,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=966939#post966939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that past life memories are interesting and I hope they aren't <b><i>gone</i></b> for 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bare mention of them in EX3 core, but details in Miracles of the Solar Exalted (MotSE). In keeping with the developers intention to shroud the First Age in more mystery, &quot;past lives&quot; don't ever manifest as vivid clear-cut memories. Rather one might experience strange dreams or evocative visions, feelings of dej\u00e0 vu, or unexplained intense emotions about resonant places. On the other hand, ancient spirits, artefacts, and </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">workings might recognise the ineffable pattern of the exaltation's heritage and react to it; for good or bad.<br /> <br /> Then there's the <b>bond</b>, which is no longer an automatic pairing between <i>every </i>solar and a lunar, but something that might have been developed by close associations over several excarnations between fated partners. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:09:41-07:00","id":966974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=966967#post966967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In keeping with the developers intention to shroud the First Age in more mystery, &quot;past lives&quot; don't ever manifest as vivid clear-cut memories. Rather one might experience strange dreams or evocative visions, feelings of dej\u00e0 vu, or unexplained intense emotions about resonant places. On the other hand, ancient spirits, artefacts, and workings might recognise the ineffable pattern of the exaltation's heritage and react to it; for good or bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems silly to me. The First Age can be as mysterious or described as the ST wants, and presumably the ST and PC decide what specifically the memories contain. I thought the point of mystery about the First Age was just to not have a canon description of it in detail, not to say that nobody anywhere knows anything about or can learn anything about it. That's silly -- it should be up to the ST.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:37:27-07:00","id":966986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars#post966918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would that actually cause the character to react. From what I have seen in the books, it never comes up at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The memories are highly different for each Exalt. In general, most of the memories tend to be dreams - when Celestial Exalted sleep, they have very vivid dream-memories about the past. These memories usually aren't terribly intrusive and not every Exalt has memories concerning the death(s) of previous incarnations. If you're interested, you might want to check out the old Caste books from First Edition - all of the Exalted in them had varying memories of the First Age. <br /> <br /> Ultimately the problem with First Age memories is that they're deeply personal and unique to each Exalt, so it's difficult to include them in general overview books of directions or subjects, and in the Scroll of Exalts there wasn't really room to include a bunch of Fist Age memories for each Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:42:05-07:00","id":966991,"title":"","content":"Plus bear in mind that solars have centuries or even millennia of memories. They aren't all going to be fixated on the shitty ten minutes at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:06:27-07:00","id":967032,"title":"","content":"I imagine it's a bit like waking up after a night of too much drinking, and gradually starting to recall what you did. Except they're not quite entirely your memories, and you only have a dim sense of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T03:16:27-07:00","id":967248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars#post966918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how you can justify starting out with several Charms right out of chargen</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think it fits better to the subject matter to start out with a few Charms because they're just things you could already do refined with some Essence.<br /> <br /> Past life memory should be prioritised on things that enhance the character one is already playing, not replacing them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:15:30-07:00","id":967930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars#post966918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I have been wondering about for a long time is just how freshly-Exalted Solars deal with the memories inherited with their exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression was previous host memories had as much influence over the Solar as the player and the ST together wanted. In my games, a lot of times previous host memories felt the same as remembering dreams although there was a noticeable distinction that allowed the Solar to know it was a memory from someone else. Also as someone above said, Solars begin play at least a year after they've exalted so they have adjusted to the memories if they have any.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars#post966918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, sure, everyone would handle things a little bit differently, but most likely the most common &quot;last memory&quot; of newly Exalted Solars is that of being hunted down and executed. No near-death experiences, narrow escapes, saves or such.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, you <u>died</u>. Violently. Via people you probably trusted.<br /> <br /> How would that actually cause the character to react. From what I have seen in the books, it never comes up at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of the previous editions, it was said that Lytek left the memories of the final moments or seconds of the Usurpation on many if not most of the shards so the newly exalted Solar would know that he or she was betrayed by the dragonblooded. Also to possibly leave a clue to the Sidereals' involvement. Though I think Arcane Fate would probably take care of those shard-impressed memories as well.<br /> <br /> Lytek was also instructed to leave some of the awesome glorious moments on there for the new host to draw inspiration from. He was also instructed to do what he could to remove the not-so-pleasant memories where the Solar was engaged in not-so-pleasant activities. This process was never 100% successful. I recall Demetheus saying with what he could remember from previous host memories, the Solars deserved to be betrayed and thrown down.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:26:50-07:00","id":967940,"title":"","content":"I have Past Incarnation memories as associative, instead of happening all at once. If something comes up that triggers the memory, then the Exalt remembers the past life memory. These memory flashes usually happens in the first century after Exaltation. After that, the Exalt doesn't encounter any new memories, though most past life memories they have already encountered have been integrated into their own memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:33:55-07:00","id":967946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=967930#post967930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was also instructed to do what he could to remove the not-so-pleasant memories where the Solar was engaged in not-so-pleasant activities. This process was never 100% successful. I recall Demetheus saying with what he could remember from previous host memories, the Solars deserved to be betrayed and thrown down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking off those particular memories entirely isn't a great idea, IMO. Learning from mistakes (your own or others') is the biggest difference between a fool and wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:50:09-07:00","id":967956,"title":"","content":"There is no set way to handle this.<br /> <br /> Past lives only affect a character (plaeyr or otherwise) if those involved want to. <br /> <br /> The Charms you begin with are not necessarily tied to your past lives. They can just be outgrowths of your own Essence that surged forward with Exaltation.<br /> <br /> If you want to portray a Solar that is overwhelmed by his Past Lives\u00b4experiences, you are free to do so. If you to play a Solar and have nothing to do with your Past Lives, you are also free to do so. Both ways are completely fine by the book.<br /> <br /> So in other words; Solars handle past lives as fitting to your drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:54:36-07:00","id":967960,"title":"","content":"Have there ever been rules for using past life memories as a tutor for learning Charms, Abilities, Spells, etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:50:46-07:00","id":967996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=967032#post967032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it's a bit like waking up after a night of too much drinking, and gradually starting to recall what you did. Except they're not quite entirely your memories, and you only have a dim sense of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This works particularly well as an analogy, because there are parts the newbie Solar will likely think are AWESOME (&quot;Holy shit, did I really strangle Mardukth?!&quot;) and parts that either inspire them to become better people or in extreme cases traumatise them for life. <br /> <br /> I forgot what Swan's Past Life rating was, but for his own good I hope it's either close to or exactly 0. <br /> <br /> But yeah, ultimately I imagine exactly how much it effects them largely comes down to the individual Solars' personalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:58:57-07:00","id":968001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=967960#post967960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have there ever been rules for using past life memories as a tutor for learning Charms, Abilities, Spells, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly as far as I know all they can do is add dice equal to the rating to dicepools. I wouldn't fault a group for implementing this as an idea, though. All I'd be concerned about is if it'd make the background a little too good compared to others since, ostensibly, the more solid kinds of mentor require more complex interaction to get at all their knowledge. <br /> <br /> Perhaps a custom ability/attribute roll would be necessary to get useful techniques out of the background, with a difficulty based on the essence requirements of those abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:04:45-07:00","id":968004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=966957#post966957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're generally fuzzy enough to not cause any real problems. A solar might somehow just <i>know</i> how to find a hidden manse or some secret cache of weapons. They might dream of lost glories and epic wars, or they might see someone and get the unshakeable sense that they know them from somewhere.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it's meant to be source of plot hooks rather than any real drama. There's already plenty of that in Creation as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in general starting characters have exalted far enough in the past that they are used to the memories but as far as being effected by them, I tend to agree with Elfive. On the other hand if considering the freshly exalted, I would think it would start as vivid dreams as you are more susceptible to a roaming mind while asleep. After a while, you would start having effects as suggested by Elfive. You would experience a lot of deja vu but unless you had some serious flaw, it would seem normal and come gradually enough to handle.<br /> <br /> As far as starting charms, I think of it along the lines of one of the Spiderman movies (all of them failed to portray Spiderman correctly except Civil War) where he wakes up from a fever and suddenly tears open the door by accident, leaps up on the wall while startled, shoots webbing without thinking about it, etc. That would be more tramatic than having a dream/vision/deja vu moment in my opinion. Especially depending on how religious you are and how indoctrinated in the evils of Anathema.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>while (horse.state == dead)<br /> {<br /> beat();<br /> }","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/830-amdramnar","name":"Amdramnar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:06:20-07:00","id":968005,"title":"","content":"Yeah, using Past Lives as a Mentor would be make Past Lives overpowered and Mentor almost useless.<br /> <br /> Now, if someone wanted to take a Past Incarnation as a Mentor (similar to Aang and Roku), I'd make them buy their Past Incarnation as Mentor and run cool vision and dream sequences as Mentor scenes. Give the interaction some substance besides &quot;Oh my character just remember how to do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> The downside of doing this is your Mentor doesn't have any status in Real Life that can help your character. But then all mentors don't have status to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-12-2016, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:36:38-07:00","id":968190,"title":"","content":"Well, there is the Infernals Past Life Background, which are much more vivid but come with the risk that every roll can get you possessed by Psycho McCrazy Solar.<br /> <br /> I could see rolling Ability + Past Life as an extended contest thing, where you have to get up to x total successes in y amount of training-downtime, but if any single roll goes too high you are possessed and have to start over at 0 successes. Maybe allow it for Solars and Lunars who take Throwback, too.<br /> <br /> EarthScorpion's rewritten Coadjutor can be a mentor for what it knows, but you have to have a high rating and an actual relationship with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I've never understood is why time spent adventuring can never count for training. Like, if I spent the past 4 months at sea captaining a ship, when I spend xp to increase Sail... I have to then dedicate non-adventuring downtime to training it. Those 4 months taught me nothing. Makes no sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-12-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:41:50-07:00","id":968195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=968190#post968190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I've never understood is why time spent adventuring can never count for training. Like, if I spent the past 4 months at sea captaining a ship, when I spend xp to increase Sail... I have to then dedicate non-adventuring downtime to training it. Those 4 months taught me nothing. Makes no sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm about 99% sure that's not how training times are supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T03:20:28-07:00","id":968438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=968190#post968190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I've never understood is why time spent adventuring can never count for training. Like, if I spent the past 4 months at sea captaining a ship, when I spend xp to increase Sail... I have to then dedicate non-adventuring downtime to training it. Those 4 months taught me nothing. Makes no sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it <b>is</b> nonsense. You don't spend xp <i>then t</i>ime; you spend xp <i>and </i>time.<br /> <br /> The time captaining at sea absolutely <i>counts </i>as training Sail. It is &quot;a significant portion of the quoted time working on the skill in question,&quot; because &quot;practical experience <i>also </i>counts as a significant amount of time training.&quot; You would, however, have to establish that you <i>also </i>spent some of that time studying your charts and almanacs, listening to advice from experienced hands, and such as &quot;neither training nor experience <i>alone</i> is sufficient for mastery.&quot; [EX3 pg 178] <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:12:06-07:00","id":968458,"title":"","content":"Welcome to Exaltation(tm)! Your one-stop resource for multigenerational cosmic power in a comfortable, versatile package!<br /> <br /> Upon first application of Exaltation(tm), you may experience feelings of existential crisis, identity uncertainty, horrible death visions, and/or a rushing feeling of misplaced invincibility. Do not fret! This is a normal result of the interaction of your consciousness with the memories of previous users. While our qualified team of gods works tirelessly to ensure the smoothest, cleanest transition possible, we nonetheless recommend a period of reestablishment and cementation of the self at your earliest convenience in order to minimize these possible side effects. <br /> <br /> *Offer limited to one per person. Exaltation(tm) only refundable in the event of death. \u200bPlease consult your local Incarna to know if Exaltation(tm) is right for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:31:38-07:00","id":968539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=968438#post968438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;neither training nor experience <i>alone</i> is sufficient for mastery.&quot; [EX3 pg 178]</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of that looked more sensible than the 2E method... except this. This makes it look like it's impossible to train anything without a tutor?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:34:31-07:00","id":968541,"title":"","content":"Why are you so pessimistic when interpreting casual language?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:07:30-07:00","id":968589,"title":"","content":"I interpret everything literally. It's even explained in my signature.<br /> What else could that sentence mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:34:26-07:00","id":968607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=968589#post968589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What else could that sentence mean?</div> </div> </div> </div> That you need to train <i>and</i> put things into practice, rather than just one or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:57:30-07:00","id":968659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=968607#post968607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That you need to train <i>and</i> put things into practice, rather than just one or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly a way of reading the sentence, and my guess is that's probably how the author intended it to be read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:13:47-07:00","id":968732,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's how I read it too. In fact that's what I would have called the &quot;literal interpretation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:55:28-07:00","id":968806,"title":"","content":"OK, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:37:19-07:00","id":968931,"title":"","content":"Past life memories tend to be triggered by like circumstances. Lyta, for example, grew up on the Isle in a dynastic family, and having failed to Exalt probably spent a lot of time being belittled and tormented by Dragon-blooded... so when she Exalted as a Dawn during sparing practice, the first thing that came rushing back were her memories of the Usurpation and the betrayal by the TerrestriaIs, and she went on a rampage. Would probably have kept right on murder-raging until the Immaculates put her down had she not been spirited away by a Sidereal. She now spends her time with a cult that tells her she's a hero and burning captured Dynasts alive with a giant magnifying glass for the glory of the Sun.<br /> <br /> Which I'd say means the answer to the original question, do past-life memories of their own violent death ever make new Solars mentally unstable, is a definitive &quot;sometimes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:40:23-07:00","id":969341,"title":"","content":"I imagine that taking an first-age God-King/Queen past life memories as a teacher would be like St. Alia of the Knife taking her memories of the Baron Harkonnen as a teacher. It could be fun for a plot hook to have solar's or infernal's with very powerful past life memories risking something akin to abomination in Dune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11426-broken-mind","name":"Broken Mind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:27:24-07:00","id":969378,"title":"","content":"Not all First Age Solars were evil or particularly crazy. (Nor all First Age Lunars and Sidereals, if you're one of those with unusually intense memories.) But IMO no past life is an actual person -- they can't change, gain new long-term memories, learn about the current age or incarnation, or adapt to new circumstances. Suddenly being a Green Sun Prince would probably especially confuse them, and it's unlikely they would grasp the idea that nearby demons and Infernals are supposed to be allies, unless they were akuma in life.<br /> <br /> I read a quest where a character with a high Past Life background got to use that as a mentor for favored MA Charms as long as she trained slowly and carefully during downtime. When she drew on memories too quickly (in non-downtime) she tended to get possessed with nasty results, including the past life eroding or building Intimacies, and using her Charms to do permanent things to her and other people. He wasn't a bad guy, but could not learn to understand that he was now low-Essence and in wildly different circumstances.<br /> <br /> It was a quest, so the ST didn't have to balance her against other PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> An alternate interpretation is that a Celestial exaltation is literally a soul, and if it retains especially strong memories it acquires the personality of whoever left the most. In that interpretation, you would have to negotiate with the dead &quot;Exalt&quot; and have an actual relationship, to convince it to teach you and maybe possess you less often. Or just shout it down to make it shut up most of the time. It would have strong opinions about other Exalted, mortals, gods, demons, how to rule the world, how you should behave, the suitability of your boyfriend... sorta like a coadjutor, or Baron Harkonnen-within. Your advantage is that you have social Charms, but the voice(s) in your head don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-14-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:48:15-07:00","id":969394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969378#post969378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all First Age Solars were evil or particularly crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, by the time of the Usurpation, First Age Solars <i>had</i> to be kind of evil and/or crazy at least to the point of jointly being threats to the continued existence of Creation itself, or else there wouldn't have really been a need for a Ursurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:54:14-07:00","id":969402,"title":"","content":"Well, a lot of Solars sure, but not every single one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:08:47-07:00","id":969409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969394#post969394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, by the time of the Usurpation, First Age Solars <i>had</i> to be kind of evil and/or crazy at least to the point of jointly being threats to the continued existence of Creation itself, or else there wouldn't have really been a need for a Ursurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was no need for an Usurpation.<br /> <br /> If there was a NEED, the Sidereals wouldn't have had to make a prophecy. They would just go and do it.<br /> <br /> Instead, what the books say is that they saw the signs of something, and got together to decide if they should do something about it, and if so, what. The corebook says that this came at the height of the 'Decadence' of the First Age. Atrocities and madness is not what is usually meant with decadence, but rather, pettyness, debauchery and lazyness. <br /> <br /> This is corroborated by all the reasons ever given for the Dragon-Blooded to revolt: they never talk of a NEED.<br /> <br /> They talk about how the Solars looked down on the DBs, how the DBs had been displaced by other servants made by the Solars...<br /> <br /> All reasons that make perfect sense, but would be the same if the Solars were completely sane and nice and wise in their rulership.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation is meant to be a complex issue, not an unavoidable tautology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:49:41-07:00","id":969434,"title":"","content":"IRC, the Prophecy was much about whether they should reform the Solars or kill them or wait it out. That's what it was needed for. The first corebook for Exalted talks about &quot;vast atrocities and terrible indulgences&quot; being already apparent.<br /> <br /> It wasn't a kind of &quot;Well, we're seeing some disturbing hints here. But only hints. So what will happen in the long term?&quot; extrapolation of a worrying trend. More of a &quot;Which of these plans to stop these obviously ruinous tyrants is the go to plan?&quot; - seeking the practical advice about which paths are available to stop an already obvious trend.<br /> <br /> Broadly, I think the Usurpation was intended to be a complex issue because you can disagree that they took the right path. Should they have killed off one of the key components for their super society (the Solars) or worked to reform them? I don't think it's intended to be complex because, we're doubting whether there was really a problem to begin with, or if it was just internal discontent and loss of prestige and displacement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:03:20-07:00","id":969438,"title":"","content":"You can have problems without having NEED: Saying the Usurpation happened because the Usurpation needed to happen cheapens the setting.<br /> <br /> And denies the Gold Faction's entire existence, considering their claim was that you did not need the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Also the actions of several other actors we are aware of who fought against the Usurpation, showing that there was no essential need for it.<br /> <br /> Again, &quot;The Usurpation happened because the Usurpation needed to happen&quot; is a tautology, and in my eyes, cheapens the setting quite a bit, and denies agency to all those who acted to make it happen.<br /> <br /> Also: Wow, my first post in six months or so and I have you sparring with me, Ghostie... seems like no matter what, I can always count on my biggest fan!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:18:13-07:00","id":969444,"title":"","content":"The Sidereal realized that things were getting bad so they held a prophecy. The Prophecy had three outcomes.<br /> <br /> In the first, the Sidereal did nothing and Creation was ultimately left a ruined wreck, civilization was gone and humanity was little more than a handful of scattered tribes left to be preyed upon by the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> The second outcome involved the Sidereal working with the Solar Exalted, and there was a 50% chance that the Creation would be destroyed as per the first vision, or the problems facing Creation would be solved and the world would enter a golden era.<br /> <br /> The third and final prophecy showed the Sidereal committing the Usurpation, an act that would diminish Creation but would ensure, with 100% surety, that Creation would survive.<br /> <br /> The important part to note note was that if the Sidereal Exalted chose to do nothing, and allowed Creation to continue on its course, and didn't take an active hand in stopping the depredations of the Solar Exalted, Creation was doomed.<br /> <br /> While perhaps the Usurpation itself was not necessary, some form of engagement on the part of the Sidereal Exalted with the Solar Exalted <i>was</i> necessary because the actions of the Solar Exalted were &quot;bad enough&quot; that left unchecked, they were going to bring about the complete ruin of Creation if nothing was done to stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-14-2016, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:20:24-07:00","id":969445,"title":"","content":"Basically, there was enough going on to inspire the Sidereals and Dragonblooded to conspire to end Solar rule, but not enough to make it unambiguously justified .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969444#post969444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The important note was that if the Sidereal Exalted chose to do nothing, and allowed Creation to continue on its course, and did nothing to stop the depredations of the Solar Exalted, Creation was doomed.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Maybe</i>. Its part of the setting that the Great Curse was undermining the Celestial Exalts, but that also means interpreting the Prophesy itself would be influenced by the Sidreals' own hubris.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-14-2016, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:29:03-07:00","id":969453,"title":"","content":"@ Colapso, er... nice to see you again? Just a coincidence, really not even a little bit personal, if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:34:37-07:00","id":969495,"title":"","content":"To be fair it isn't like the Gold Faction now is the same as the Gold Faction of the Usurpation. That one was whether or not to do anything and how to handle the Solars. The black prophecy established not doing anything was bad, gold was your high risk high reward, but bronze was the safe bet and it became the option it went with. The new gold faction is whether or not to use the Solars who are reappearing, not whether the previous decision was right, just &quot;Hey we've got a crapton of problems and we've Solars again, maybe we can use them to lighten our workload by throwing them at the problems.&quot; <br /> <br /> I will also point out that whether or not Bronze was the correct isn't decided by saying that doing something was necessary. Cause the world is guaranteed saved in Bronze, but if one wants to be optimistic the world can be so much better if they strived for good option in the Gold. One could argue that the Sids choose the easy route and in a way lazy by not taking the chance. It's still viable to say the Bronze and Gold were correct, and there's always the option that something in the Great Curse caused the Sids to do or overlook something that could have been even better than what they did do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:04:29-07:00","id":969614,"title":"","content":"They overlooked to ask <i><b>how long</b></i> the world would remain saved before being destroyed anyway, and if it would also be saved from all those things outside of Fate that their 100% voluntary, non-samsara Prophecy could not in the slightest degree predict or take account of. They just assumed they already knew everything.<br /> <br /> Except that, like the Solars and Lunars, not all of them were elders up to their eyebrows in craaaazy lunatic mode. Some of the younger ones might have said &quot;Wait a minute, haven't we forgotten...&quot; and been drowned out or ignored. Or maybe not, since their Curse gets worse in groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> To get back to the past life question, it's likely that the more memories you have in your Exaltation, the longer your past life lived before dying, and the crazier they probably became. So if your memories are especially intrusive, or frequently threaten to possess you, your past life was probably crazy, even if it wasn't obvious on a day-to-day basis. If your best-remembered past life was still mostly sane, they may have died young for a Celestial, and also have less influence on your current life. Alternately, you could have had a very long-lived crazy whose memories were scrubbed out especially aggressively. I'm sure that when an akuma dies, Lytek takes exra effort to remove <i><b>everything</b></i>. (And then was/is politically 'discouraged' from mentioning the existence of Solar and Lunar akuma back then, or mentioning Sidereal akuma now.)<br /> <br /> Crazy doesn't have to mean evil, though. Misho in Keychain of Creation has a believably crazy First Age incarnation, but not in an oppressive-tyrant or destroying-the-world way. The man was a workaholic, spent most of his life obsessed with immortality, and finally killed himself to create an immortality mcguffin, and he can't handle the sight of blood. He's a very nice guy, but imagine having him freaking out in the back your head while you're trying to survive a battle.<br /> <br /> However, for non-Infernals there's the possibility of having not <i><b>one</b></i> particularly vivid past life, but a bunch of scattered memories from several past incarnations, jumbled together confusingly. Possibly with jumbled bits of contradictory personalities left from multiple people. What psychological effect would <i><b>that</b></i> have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-14-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:40:34-07:00","id":969632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969614#post969614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They overlooked to ask <i><b>how long</b></i> the world would remain saved before being destroyed anyway, and if it would also be saved from all those things outside of Fate that their 100% voluntary, non-samsara Prophecy could not in the slightest degree predict or take account of. They just assumed they already knew everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that the entire premise of Exalted, the Usurpation and almost the entirety of the Sidereal player experience are ruined if the takeaway is, &quot;The Great Prophecy was never accurate or credible to begin with and the Sidereal were complete, blithering morons for following it.&quot; Really, when the Sidereal's were on par with the Three Stooges in concerns of the Prophecy, and the Prophecy and subsequent Usurpation is supposed to be the cornerstone of Exalted's setting, that doesn't really set a good tone for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:52:35-07:00","id":969639,"title":"","content":"I forget where, but I'm pretty sure there's been an angle of &quot;Creation will last at least another Age&quot;. But yes, applying a ton of things to try and discredit the Great Prophecy does a disservice to the setting for no gain. The Great Prophecy and the Usurpation are more plot device than anything; the intent behind them is &quot;We need a reason the Solars were gone and the world was lessened so they can return as great heroes&quot;, and the sidereals happen to be written into a uniquely applicable position for such a purpose.<br /> <br /> In my estimation, the Vision of Gold mostly exists for a what-if? scenario of playing Sidereals attempting the Vision of Gold before the Usurpation occurs, more than any true &quot;This is an objectively correct path&quot;. If nothing else, it's a weighting of averages.<br /> <br /> I make you a bet. Russian Roulette. If you hit a bullet you die. If you hit an empty chamber, you walk out a millionaire. How many chambers need to be empty for this bet to be worth it?<br /> <br /> Now let's step it up. If you die, I will hunt down your family and kill them. If you live, your entire family is prosperous and happy. Does this alter the number of chambers that need to be empty? I mean it's good for your entire family if you win, but... if you lose, everyone you love dies as well.<br /> <br /> Let's step it up again. If you die, I make the sun go supernova. Everyone dies. If you win, the world magically becomes prosperous and glorious. Does this alter the number of chambers that need to be empty for this to sound like a fair deal?<br /> <br /> The way I've always seen the Vision of Gold, it was always unfavorable odds. If you'll only risk it with one bullet loaded, there's three. If you'll risk 50/50 odds, there's 4 or 5 bullets. If you're okay with one empty chamber, the revolver is fully loaded and you have to hope for a factory defect on a bullet. It was a long-shot, one that would have reaped unimaginable wonders if it succeeded, but which was fraught with peril and would doom the entire world on failure.<br /> <br /> A path only PCs would pursue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:57:19-07:00","id":969657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969632#post969632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that the entire premise of Exalted, the Usurpation and almost the entirety of the Sidereal player experience are ruined if the takeaway is, &quot;The Great Prophecy was never accurate or credible to begin with and the Sidereal were complete, blithering morons for following it.&quot; Really, when the Sidereal's were on par with the Three Stooges in concerns of the Prophecy, and the Prophecy and subsequent Usurpation is supposed to be the cornerstone of Exalted's setting, that doesn't really set a good tone for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! That's why I'm so unhappy with the way Sidereals are written.<br /> But I can't pretend it isn't written that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:31:45-07:00","id":969670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969657#post969657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed! That's why I'm so unhappy with the way Sidereals are written.<br /> But I can't pretend it isn't written that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't really say they're being stupid with the prophecies though. I mean the Rhaksha, demons, and ghosts don't show up in Fate, so even if they followed up Bronze with &quot;How long will that peace last?&quot; Nothing was going to show up. I mean one could argue that was part of the point of making the prophecy about not doing anything. One find out if the situation is going to improve on it's own, two how bad would the situation get in a vacuum. They can't account for things outside the system, but there's definitely a bit of a difference between the world is going to get a little screwed up and the world will be totally obliterated. So as soon as they get the sign that says &quot;If left to their own devices the world will become something we can generously call a hellhole on it's best day.&quot; Well what are the odds that the Rhaksha will improve the situation on not doing anything, and they still had the Incarnae and the other gods and elementals if anything happened it was going to be a harder fight, but something like the Balorean Crusade had never happened before so they were blindsided by it. The Great Contagion was designed by the Deathlords, and nothing like them had ever existed, so can't reasonably say the Sids were being stupid for not anticipating a super disease cooked up by super exalt ghosts was going to happen. The Yozi are dealt with 3CD are the worst that are coming out and those were a known commodity with methods of dealing with them being available. <br /> <br /> Just my little issue with people arguing the Sids were being idiots with the Great Prophecies since there are blindspots in their ability to prophesize. And if anyone wants to bring up Samsara I will point out that first I don't know if the Sids know the Maidens have that, but as far as anyone who knows is concerned it also binds the viewers to what they see meaning for all they would know looking into it would bind them to a terrible option even if they didn't want it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:51:12-07:00","id":969734,"title":"","content":"The thing for me is that if your choice of the Prophecy is ostensibly between <br /> <br /> a1) safety or b1) glory<br /> <br /> and then you go &quot;Actually choosing b), glory, might make us safer after all, because we need defenders of against all the things we can't account for in your model&quot; then that transforms your choices into a2) maybe more safety, b2) glory+maybe more safety.<br /> <br /> And I can see why people might think then a2 is the choice for &quot;chumps&quot; against b2.<br /> <br /> But this is what we get from Sidereals not being able to see out of Fate, and out of Fate being chock of dangerous, apocalyptic stuff which the game is sets up Solars to handle.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this is all without the nuance of, maybe for human reasons and immediacy of threats offered by each path, you might choose a2 over b2. I feel like there should be more than that, myself.<br /> <br /> My preference is subvert it by saying that, yes, forces outside of Fate can possible offset the safety offered by the Bronze, yes, but also could be harnessed to provide the glory promised by the Gold (without the Solar Exalted). That gets us back to choosing between two choices that are balanced and not dominated by the other. But in my experience as an Exalted fan, absolutely no one else I've encountered ever has liked the idea of that, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:36:29-07:00","id":969757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969670#post969670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't really say they're being stupid with the prophecies though. I mean the Rhaksha, demons, and ghosts don't show up in Fate, so even if they followed up Bronze with &amp;quot;How long will that peace last?&amp;quot; Nothing was going to show up. I mean one could argue that was part of the point of making the prophecy about not doing anything. One find out if the situation is going to improve on it's own, two how bad would the situation get in a vacuum. They can't account for things outside the system, but there's definitely a bit of a difference between the world is going to get a little screwed up and the world will be totally obliterated. So as soon as they get the sign that says &amp;quot;If left to their own devices the world will become something we can generously call a hellhole on it's best day.&amp;quot; Well what are the odds that the Rhaksha will improve the situation on not doing anything, and they still had the Incarnae and the other gods and elementals if anything happened it was going to be a harder fight, but something like the Balorean Crusade had never happened before so they were blindsided by it. The Great Contagion was designed by the Deathlords, and nothing like them had ever existed, so can't reasonably say the Sids were being stupid for not anticipating a super disease cooked up by super exalt ghosts was going to happen. The Yozi are dealt with 3CD are the worst that are coming out and those were a known commodity with methods of dealing with them being available. <br /> <br /> Just my little issue with people arguing the Sids were being idiots with the Great Prophecies since there are blindspots in their ability to prophesize. And if anyone wants to bring up Samsara I will point out that first I don't know if the Sids know the Maidens have that, but as far as anyone who knows is concerned it also binds the viewers to what they see meaning for all they would know looking into it would bind them to a terrible option even if they didn't want it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also there's the point that all the things outside fate that were known of were at the time basically non issues.<br /> <br /> The raksha were disparate actors concerned only with individual glory and devouring souls; the idea of their putting aside their personal stories in pursuit of a grand destruction of Creation was ridiculous.<br /> <br /> The neverborn were slumbering Titans whose nightmares shook the underworld but never reached the surface. What few actors they had to affect the surface were rare and ultimately possible to handle (hekatonkhires and wraiths)<br /> <br /> The yozi were long banished and trapped. Their only influence in creation was demons who slipped through the cracks, demons who were summoned, and mad servants trading volition for power. All of which would be lessened by the lack of Solars - no one can summon Ligier, therefore he won't be present.<br /> <br /> And then in 2e plot line, the ridiculous happened -- the neverborn acted and empowered ghosts of Solars who encouraged the Balorian crusade and unleashed a grand contagion upon Creation (facts that are still not known to the wider setting; the contagion came from somewhere, the raksha invaded, but the why is only known to us because of omniscient narration.), The yozi and neverborn broke the prison and came into possession of Solar level actors to inflict their rage on Creation.<br /> <br /> Calling the sidereals idiots for not expecting this is like calling farmers idiots for not predicting the rise of super intelligent psychic cows - it was completely beyond even mundane prediction, much less the blind spots of fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:05:55-07:00","id":969965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969757#post969757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The raksha were disparate actors concerned only with individual glory and devouring souls; the idea of their putting aside their personal stories in pursuit of a grand destruction of Creation was ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh... I tried to resist being pulled into this derail, but I have failed my Temperance roll. I want to respond to just this.<br /> <br /> The Raksha made a major invasion of Creation very soon after the Primordial War, seeing Creation weakened without its former defenders at the helm. The combined, united Exalted host beat them back, and eventually the Solars extracted Oaths from the Raksha never to attack Creation again. Those Oaths, which prevented further invasions for the rest of the First Age, were only valid as long as the Solar Deliberative ruled Creation.<br /> <br /> Then a free Primordial attacked Creation, and again the Exalted worked together to hold him back. He was only finally defeated by Solars wielding the Sword of Creation. And the Exalted knew there was at least one other hostile Primordial still out there.<br /> <br /> The Yozis are bound, but their souls periodically slip into Creation. Who can cast Adamant Banishment? Only a Solar. Who can cast Sapphire Banishment? Only a Lunar, or one of the &lt;100 already-overworked Sidereals. How many Dragon-Blooded or Sidereal lives should be sacrificed to chase Ligier or Munaxes or Erembour back to Malfeas the hard way?<br /> Only a Solar can summon a Third Circle demon deliberately into Creation, which is probably something the Vision of Gold didn't entirely account for.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals knew all this. The older ones had lived through all of those events.<br /> <br /> The Vision of Bronze is only '100%, guaranteed victory, nothing can possibly ever go wrong, Creation is 100% perfectly safe forever and ever' when pretending things outside of Fate don't exist and assuming that the Vision extends infinite time into the future. When considering all available information -- which is common sense when making important, world-changing decisions -- the Vision of Bronze assures Creation's survival no better than the Vision of Gold. The two Visions were equally risky for Creation. If the Prophecy doesn't account for all variables, well, Exalted can think for themselves too.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see is the Sidereals all being perfectly aware that threats outside of Fate mean that the Vision of Bronze is not 100% guaranteed safety, but as far as they knew approximately as risky as the Vision of Gold. Not having any clear-cut numerical risk-assessment, leaving room for intelligent, decent people to argue that their side is <i><b>slightly</b></i> less risky, without being dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:47:26-07:00","id":969994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969965#post969965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh... I tried to resist being pulled into this derail, but I have failed. I want to respond to just this.<br /> <br /> The Raksha made a major invasion of Creation very soon after the Primordial War, seeing Creation weakened without its former defenders at the helm. The combined, united Exalted host beat them back, and eventually the Solars extracted Oaths from the Raksha never to attack Creation again. Those Oaths, which prevented further invasions for the rest of the First Age, were only valid as long as the Solar Deliberative ruled Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except the Rhaksha couldn't come back in force without an invitation. It's why in 2nd First and Forsaken Lion went out and invited them in. Even with the Great Contagion killing the world they didn't come back until Balor rallied them and they got the invitation, so at the very least the Rhaksha seemed to consider them valid for a long time after the Solars started being dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969965#post969965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then a free Primordial attacked Creation, and again the Exalted worked together to hold him back. He was only finally defeated by Solars wielding the Sword of Creation. And the Exalted knew there was at least one other hostile Primordial still out there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah not like they didn't still have the Imperial Manse, or the Incarnae, or at least one Primordial still on their side. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969965#post969965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yozis are bound, but their souls periodically slip into Creation. Who can cast Adamant Banishment? Only a Solar. Who can cast Sapphire Banishment? Only a Lunar, or one of the &lt;100 already-overworked Sidereals. How many Dragon-Blooded or Sidereal lives should be sacrificed to chase Ligier or Munaxes or Erembour back to Malfeas the hard way?<br /> Only a Solar can summon a Third Circle demon deliberately into Creation, which is probably something the Vision of Gold didn't entirely account for.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except without the Solars a 3CD is almost never showing up and most of the time their interested in their own pursuits more than anything else. Again they were willing to throw whatever to end those threats. It was always acknowledged they were going to have a harder time with major threats. Plus from what we've got in 3rd those banishment spells don't exist, so that really isn't viable now a days. <br /> <br /> All of this should have been very obvious to the Sidereals. But... they didn't care.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969965#post969965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vision of Bronze is only '100%, guaranteed victory, nothing can possibly ever go wrong, Creation is 100% perfectly safe forever and ever' when pretending things outside of Fate don't exist and assuming that the Vision extends infinite time into the future. Trying to consider all available information -- which is common sense when making important, world-changing decisions -- the Vision of Bronze assures Creation's survival no better than the Vision of Gold. If the Prophecy doesn't account for all variables, well, Exalted can think for themselves too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh please it was never &quot;Nothing will ever go wrong again the world is perfectly safe forever and ever.&quot; It was, &quot;Well we had to take your legs, but you're still alive.&quot; They saw what happened if they didn't do anything to deal with the Solars, which left them with the old standby of make the Solars fix it, or launch a coup against the Solars. Heck read the entries on the prophecies in 2nd again, the vision of Bronze technically doesn't account the Jade Prison that was an idea they figured out after the visions to deal with Bronze's forever war against the Solars. And no Gold was not equally likely to make the world as safe as Bronze because Gold included repeated mentions of if anything goes wrong it all goes to pot. It's why Yuurei compared it to high stakes Russian roulette.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:57:58-07:00","id":970127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969965#post969965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Raksha made a major invasion of Creation very soon after the Primordial War, seeing Creation weakened without its former defenders at the helm. The combined, united Exalted host beat them back, and eventually the Solars extracted Oaths from the Raksha never to attack Creation again. Those Oaths, which prevented further invasions for the rest of the First Age, were only valid as long as the Solar Deliberative ruled Creation.<br /> <br /> Then a free Primordial attacked Creation, and again the Exalted worked together to hold him back. He was only finally defeated by Solars wielding the Sword of Creation. And the Exalted knew there was at least one other hostile Primordial still out there.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a lot of setting creep here that didn't exist when the Great Prophecy was first established as part of the lore. I expect if we'd kept the focus on the distant past we'd probably have at least picked up some proto-Deathlords.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:05:48-07:00","id":970135,"title":"","content":"While I don't have a link available, Holden said years ago in another discussion about Sidereal and the Great Prophecy, that the Blind Seers sidebar in First Edition was one of the more disempowering segments of the Exalted gameline and hinted that people shouldn't assume that the Great Prophecy (or the Sidereal Exalted) will work like that in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:14:09-07:00","id":970323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970135#post970135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't have a link available, Holden said years ago in another discussion about Sidereal and the Great Prophecy, that the Blind Seers sidebar in First Edition was one of the more disempowering segments of the Exalted gameline and hinted that people shouldn't assume that the Great Prophecy (or the Sidereal Exalted) will work like that in 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is great. The &quot;LOL THEY DIDN'T SEE LOLOLOLLOOOOL ROFLMAO&quot; got spammed SO hard, SO frequently in 2e, that Sidereals were more defined by their consistent, endless FAILURE to see and predict things than any actual visionary talent. That button got pounded basically every opportunity that arose to laugh at Sidereals.<br /> <br /> I feel that the Vision of Bronze vs Vision of Gold needs to actually be &quot;99% surety of NOT destroying all Creation, <b>after</b> the unknown factors, in exchange for lessening it, to survive another Age&quot; versus &quot;Well, it's a huge gamble, big risk, unlikely odds, uncomfortably likely to fail, one in a few thousand chance of success, but if we win, we win BIG and the world is saved for perpetuity and we're the big damn heroes for doing it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not this &quot;100% vs 99%&quot;.or &quot;99% vs 98.999%&quot;, &quot;the Vision of Gold was totally something that rational intelligent people would think was adequately likely to succeed, but the Bronze was just a LIIIIIITTLE SMIIIIIIIIDGE more likely so the Sidereals CHUMPED OUT like COWARDS&quot;. In order for it to be &quot;a grim necessity, undertaken&quot; and not &quot;cowardly spineless simpering&quot; the Vision of Gold needs to be adequately unlikely to succeed that the idea of pushing this button and probably ending the world is more the act of a madman than a bold impetuous and just move.<br /> <br /> Unless your goal is &quot;the Bronze plan was objectively and completely wrong in every way&quot;, there had to be serious, significant risks to the Gold plan, and a near-absolute guarantee of safety to Bronze even after all dangers factored in. It can't be &quot;I roll a d20. The Bronze plan fails on a 1 and the Gold plan fails on a 1-2.&quot;, without going for &quot;everything sucks forever but at least we all live, 95% guaranteed&quot; being criminally negligent compared to &quot;Everything is grand and glorious forever, 90% guaranteed&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only &quot;gain&quot; I see from playing down the dangers of the Vision of Gold is making the Sidereals look less competent as sages and prophets, sabotaging their thesis.... and for what? How is making them look less competent a good thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 09-15-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:52:18-07:00","id":970349,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there some write up online where the vision of Gold lead to Solars mentally dominating Creation. They were the mad blood thirsty gods who did horrible things and you thanked them for it. <br /> <br /> I think Jena Moran wrote it up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:32:10-07:00","id":970679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars#post966918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I have been wondering about for a long time is just how freshly-Exalted Solars deal with the memories inherited with their exaltation.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, part of the package of Exaltation is that you also receive some memories from your &quot;past lives&quot;. This is how you can justify starting out with several Charms right out of chargen, but what about the actual RP-ing aspect of this? Does it just never come up in your games?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, everyone would handle things a little bit differently, but most likely the most common &quot;last memory&quot; of newly Exalted Solars is that of being hunted down and executed. No near-death experiences, narrow escapes, saves or such.<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, you <u>died</u>. Violently. Via people you probably trusted.<br /> <br /> How would that actually cause the character to react. From what I have seen in the books, it never comes up at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answering this question authoritatively will only remove agency from the PCs and reduce choice for the players. If I declare that Solars experience their betrayal and death from their past lives, then I'm setting them all up for what amounts to revenge fantasy or potential mental illness. I'm telling each and every Solar player that their character is a victim right out of the gate. That's a bad call for an empowerment fantasy.<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, I declare that Solars aren't affected by their memories in such a fashion, then I'm removing potential interesting sub-plots for PCs. Maybe one of my players really wanted to have these traumatic dreams of being murdered by a Sidereal, find that Sid in the present day, and get revenge.<br /> <br /> Solars are also intended to be the blank-slate Exalts. I'm also not a dick ST who writes my players' characters. Given all of the above, I conclude that individual Solars are affected by their past lives as determined by the Solars' player, no more and no less.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:32:07-07:00","id":970714,"title":"","content":"I'd say sometimes a little less is acceptable, if the player's indulged in some of the more toxic memes brewed by the fandom. It's less &quot;writing your player's character,&quot; and more &quot;keeping a guiding hand on the portrayal of the setting.&quot; <br /> <br /> (Don't get me wrong, a character being essentially overwritten by his past existence can be a fun story to explore, but if someone brings that to me as his or her first character in the setting, I'm most likely gonna explain why that's atypical and try and work with them to produce something that fits a little better, or at least justify why they're different.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:38:50-07:00","id":970719,"title":"","content":"On the Gold Faction, I don't trust them. I am almost certain that they're pulling a Sun Li(from Jade Empire) stratagem. Let the Solars do the work of fixing the world, then backstabbing them in a specially prepared/inflicted weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:46:45-07:00","id":970724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970719#post970719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Gold Faction, I don't trust them. I am almost certain that they're pulling a Sun Li(from Jade Empire) stratagem. Let the Solars do the work of fixing the world, then backstabbing them in a specially prepared/inflicted weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a possibility from your ST. There's also the possibility that they're honest in their desire to harness the power of the Solars, while keeping them from getting out of control and making baby-press pipe organs [&quot;the trick is replacing the babies with the right size to produce the right note after they grow too old or die from being pressed into screaming&quot;] or whatever other insanity they decide hey, this sounds like fun, let's do it. Or just having epic duels that destroy swaths of landscape and leave the land incapable of supporting life for centuries. You know, the sorts of shenanigans bored people with too much power get up to.<br /> <br /> So I would caution against blind distrust as surely as I would blind trust, basically. &quot;Trust, but verify&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:59:25-07:00","id":970728,"title":"","content":"You really think the usurpation is something that would work <i>twice</i>? Nah, if the solars wind up ruling the world and going crazy again, it's fucked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:18:25-07:00","id":970766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970714#post970714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say sometimes a little less is acceptable, if the player's indulged in some of the more toxic memes brewed by the fandom. It's less &quot;writing your player's character,&quot; and more &quot;keeping a guiding hand on the portrayal of the setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Don't get me wrong, a character being essentially overwritten by his past existence can be a fun story to explore, but if someone brings that to me as his or her first character in the setting, I'm most likely gonna explain why that's atypical and try and work with them to produce something that fits a little better, or at least justify why they're different.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I think a PC concept is unhelpful/unacceptable, I'll veto it, or provide assistance massaging it into something acceptable. I'm never going to be comfortable making affirmative pronouncements about the emotional impact of something on a PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:27:35-07:00","id":970769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970728#post970728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really think the usurpation is something that would work <i>twice</i>? Nah, if the solars wind up ruling the world and going crazy again, it's fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's generally been the stance I've taken for pragmatic Immaculate and Bronze Faction characters.<br /> Was the Usurpation correct? It doesn't matter. If the Solars regain a foothold we're probably more likely to have a thousand year rampage of revenge than a new golden age and for every Solar who insists they're better than that there's a sliding scale from &quot;we need them but I'll probably never trust them&quot; to &quot;Dragon-Blooded! Do they even have SOULS!?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:01:06-07:00","id":970785,"title":"","content":"Yes. I think it's going to hard for Solars to ever be able to <i>truly</i> trust the Sidereal Exalted ever again, especially once they find out that the Sidereals were responsible for the Usurpation - this is a huge flaw in the presentation of the Gold Faction's ideology, and was only magnified by the fact that they wouldn't tell the Illuminated Solars they were behind the Usurpation. So when the Illuminated Solars (inevitably) discover the truth, it's going to create an unbreachable wall between them and the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Hopefully 3rd edition changes this up with the Gold Faction Sidereal doing something like bluntly telling the reborn Solars, &quot;Yeah, some of our kind participated and helped plan the Usurpation. They are, and were, assholes. And while that fact may cause some trust issues, remember that those other assholes want to murder your ass. We simply want you to rule justly and fairly like you're supposed to. It's up to you if you want to keep working with us or go your own way.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:31:25-07:00","id":970800,"title":"","content":"I would probably tend to agree about Usurpation 2 being a canceled sequel.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's the case that, y'know, the Solars are just so overwhelmingly good at what they do that they would crush any Usurpation 2. Everyone else is quite good, you know.<br /> <br /> But unless they're about as alienating to every possible ally as they were last time, it's going to be a long and bloody stalemate, as the Solars gather their supporters, and the fight drags on indefinitely. Then you've got powers outside Creation poised to wreak havoc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:47:49-07:00","id":970806,"title":"","content":"There's also the idea that Heaven isn't about to let Lytek get mugged again, so Usurpation 2.0 is going to face the same problem the Primordials did: how do you stop 600 or so godkings that reincarnate as fast as you can kill them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:12:15-07:00","id":970820,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's only like 100 this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:19:46-07:00","id":970828,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting moral dilemma. Should an Exalt be judged based on the actions of their previous incarnation? Should an entire Exalted host be judged by the actions of a few (or most) members? The Bronze faction Sidereals of the Usurpation certainly believed so. <br /> <br /> The first question is explored a bit by a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dax_(Star_Trek:_Deep_Space_Nine)\" target=\"_blank\">Deep Space Nine</a> episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:49:24-07:00","id":970849,"title":"","content":"Actually the Sidereals spent a long time keeping an eye on all the solars, all of them would inevitably go mad no exception. The original gold faction Sidereals didn't refute the solars madness but argued that setting up an inter-exalted policing system was a better alternative and dragon-blooded ruling creation was just a way of creation dying slowly. Neither side was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:21:24-07:00","id":970872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970828#post970828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting moral dilemma. Should an Exalt be judged based on the actions of their previous incarnation? Should an entire Exalted host be judged by the actions of a few (or most) members? The Bronze faction Sidereals of the Usurpation certainly believed so.<br /> <br /> The first question is explored a bit by a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dax_(Star_Trek:_Deep_Space_Nine)\" target=\"_blank\">Deep Space Nine</a> episode.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That dilemma is also excellent plot-hook material - both for Solar and Lunar players, if they're plagued with memories of past glories or horrors, or being judged for actions from a past life... or for sid players who are forced to decide on this issue as judge and possibly executioner","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:33:53-07:00","id":970879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970872#post970872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That dilemma is also excellent plot-hook material - both for Solar and Lunar players, if they're plagued with memories of past glories or horrors, or being judged for actions from a past life... or for sid players who are forced to decide on this issue as judge and possibly executioner</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine end game Solars/Lunars may want to put a Sidereal on trial too. Though Arcane Fate would make having a fair trial difficult. I imagine some character may not want a trial at all because of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:10:34-07:00","id":970908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970828#post970828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting moral dilemma. Should an Exalt be judged based on the actions of their previous incarnation? Should an entire Exalted host be judged by the actions of a few (or most) members? The Bronze faction Sidereals of the Usurpation certainly believed so.<br /> <br /> The first question is explored a bit by a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dax_(Star_Trek:_Deep_Space_Nine)\" target=\"_blank\">Deep Space Nine</a> episode.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that the Bronze Faction is &quot;judging&quot; the modern Solars for the crimes their past incarnations committed. Rather, they held a Prophecy that said the only way, 100% to save the world without the risk of its destruction, would be to murder every Solar and Lunar and continue to murder them forever. If you ever stopped doing that, then there would be a risk that the world would be destroyed. The Bronze Faction felt that they had the duty to Creation to do shoulder that burden and engage in the Usurpation, even though presumably many members were friends or lovers of the Solar and Lunar Exalted. They were simply the faction that put their &quot;job&quot; ahead of their personal feelings and idealistic thinking.<br /> <br /> When the Bronze Faction leads a Wyld Hunt against a Solar, they probably just think it's bad luck on the part of the mortal who received a Solar Exaltation - sucks to be them, now they have to be killed even though they probably didn't do anything to deserve death. <br /> <br /> That said, Solars being held accountable for the actions of their past incarnations or, on the flip side, holding others accountable for the actions they took against that Solar's past incarnation, can absolutely make good plot hooks. A Solar can walk into a Fair Folk Court and, by virtue of his past life, demand the fealty of the gathered Fair Folk due to an oath they swore, but at the same time, the Solar may have to deal with people who are unhappy with actions his past incarnation took - it's basically a two way street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:32:44-07:00","id":971358,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't fathom Usurpation 2.0, because I can't imagine 1,000+ Celestials and 10,000+ Terrestrials, all from different backgrounds and with different goals, to group up based on their type and start going at each other. Ex3 Lunars have what amounts to a loose coalition fighting the Realm, and even that is strictly voluntary because they can't unite around that goal.<br /> <br /> I can't imagine a world where Yurgen Kaneko, Perfect Soul, and Panther sit down and agree on a unified plan for dominating Creation. Yurgen can't even get Samea 100% on board with his goals, and Panther is likely to punch anybody who tries going into full god-king mode. Meanwhile, PS is more likely to see the Bull's army as just one more invasive, conquering horde not that different from the Realm.<br /> <br /> It's a mistake to assume absolutist tribalism among any of the Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:57:53-07:00","id":971476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970908#post970908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that the Bronze Faction is &quot;judging&quot; the modern Solars for the crimes their past incarnations committed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this, yes. The Bronze Faction aren't, or at least shouldn't be written as if, they're murdering Random Joe Mortal #751,682 who just happens to be glowing gold because he ostensibly did something terrible, in the past life of his exalted spirit, over two thousand years ago.<br /> <br /> They're killing him because the risk is too great that he'll do one of 1) go mad again, or 2) find out about the Usurpation and go on a roaring rampage of revenge, after accumulating enough power that he can't be put down and will plunge Creation into war and chaos all around him.<br /> <br /> The Bronze feels that the madness is apparently endemic to the Solar condition, and that it is either incurable or too risky to cure given their prodigious potential for talent at deception and violence, and thus they must continue to purge the Solars to prevent them from potentially dooming Creation once more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:16:46-07:00","id":971854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=969632#post969632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that the entire premise of Exalted, the Usurpation and almost the entirety of the Sidereal player experience are ruined if the takeaway is, &quot;The Great Prophecy was never accurate or credible to begin with and the Sidereal were complete, blithering morons for following it.&quot; Really, when the Sidereal's were on par with the Three Stooges in concerns of the Prophecy, and the Prophecy and subsequent Usurpation is supposed to be the cornerstone of Exalted's setting, that doesn't really set a good tone for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, indeed, the cornerstone of the Usurpation is <b><i>the Great Curse</i></b>, and that is not <i>meant </i>to set a good tone.<br /> <br /> In EX2, the solar (and lunar) exalts' Great Curse manifested as the Flawed Virtues which drove them to increasingly irrational actions, which prompted the sidereal exalts to gather together to contemplate their options. However, the sidereal exalts were <i>themselves </i>subject to their own version of the Great Curse: Flawed Fates, which fated them to advocate or adopt unwise actions and then rationalise this as their own meritorious choice. Their tendency to Limit Break, of course, increased when they gathered together in numbers and this was <i>explicitly </i>presented as the reason so many advocated for the bronze solution rather than the gold.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse is still with us in EX3, though with somewhat improved playability for solars. I rather hope sidereal exalts get a much more <i>clear </i>Great Curse mechanic in EX3.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:16:19-07:00","id":971868,"title":"","content":"I think you can go down that route that the Great Curse drove all Exalted to their decisions at the close of the First Age - so you have the Dragonblooded being pushed by elemental passions to make a decision that might not be right, etc. And that''s fine.<br /> <br /> But I think if it was very strongly of that tone, I do feel like it could fee like a lot of unsympathetic people making bad decisions. I think you want to keep at least some nobility and rationality of purpose there to the Usurpation. It's particularly what allows the failures of the Second Age to feel sympathetic and have pathos.<br /> <br /> I'd would like Sidereals to have a more multifaceted Great Curse in 3e, as well as clear. Then make it like the Solar one, so it's appropriate to the story conditions at the time.<br /> <br /> I personally think it would be cool to have some alternatives along the theme of &quot;Trapped by Attachment&quot;. So you've got your Rakan Thulios who get attached by love and rage against fate denying them, and your &quot;Flawlessly Loyal Advisor&quot; who gets attached to a Solar prodigy and won't hear a word said against them even as they become increasingly destructive and contrary to fate. All these attachments that they form that directly impede and erode their purpose as impartial guardians of humanity.<br /> <br /> You can keep the hubristic curses as well of course, however I really like the idea of their intimacies undermining their ability to do their job. Excesses of loyalty, humility, love, that are not suited to their role as detached bureaucrats for the good of all.<br /> <br /> Probably you guys have other ideas? Basically just making it more multifaceted than &quot;Sidereals have hubris and fixations&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:11:00-07:00","id":971899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970879#post970879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine end game Solars/Lunars may want to put a Sidereal on trial too. Though Arcane Fate would make having a fair trial difficult. I imagine some character may not want a trial at all because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> arcane fate only makes it impossible for the rest of heaven to prove anything<br /> <br /> the solars and lunars would - with a little work - be able to personally testify &quot;That's the fellow there who killed my last incarnation, I saw it myself&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:06:47-07:00","id":971953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=971854#post971854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, indeed, the cornerstone of the Usurpation is <b><i>the Great Curse</i></b>, and that is not <i>meant </i>to set a good tone.<br /> <br /> In EX2, the solar (and lunar) exalts' Great Curse manifested as the Flawed Virtues which drove them to increasingly irrational actions, which prompted the sidereal exalts to gather together to contemplate their options. However, the sidereal exalts were <i>themselves </i>subject to their own version of the Great Curse: Flawed Fates, which fated them to advocate or adopt unwise actions and then rationalise this as their own meritorious choice. Their tendency to Limit Break, of course, increased when they gathered together in numbers and this was <i>explicitly </i>presented as the reason so many advocated for the bronze solution rather than the gold.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse is still with us in EX3, though with somewhat improved playability for solars. I rather hope sidereal exalts get a much more <i>clear </i>Great Curse mechanic in EX3.]</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've said before when this comes up, I feel that if the Sidereal's decision to ultimately choose to go with the Bronze Vision rather than the Gold Vision comes down to, <i>not</i> an incredibly careful consideration of the odds, <i>not</i> a deeply weighed sense of what is best for the future of Creation, <i>not</i> even the different arguments between the cynical and rational vs idealistic and hopeful, <i>nor</i> even long debates and discussions with one another, but instead comes down to, &quot;The Sidereal choose the Bronze Prophecy because the Great Curse made them,&quot; that is splat ruining.<br /> <br /> The Great Prophecy and the arguments over which path to take is arguably the single most defining moment of the Sidereal Exalted, and it's supposed to be an argument that still has powerful implications even in the 2nd Age. To attribute the result of that argument to the Great Curse rather than the actual judgement of the Sidereal Exalted hurts the Sidereal and turns them into a joke. It's the same as when the game line says that the Great Prophecy was completely flawed from the get-go because the Sidereal Exalted never realized that there are beings who are outside of Fate even though hunting down creatures to whom Fate does not apply is their <i>job</i> and one they do with some frequency.<br /> <br /> Or to put it another way, it would kind of be like if the game said that Empress designed the Realm's political and social system to be devious and twisted, not because the Empress wanted to carefully balance everything to collapse if she were to fall and wanted to both prevent her assassination and spitefully ensure that if anyone did kill her they'd be faced with a collapsing empire, but rather she set up the Realm's political and social system the way she did because, &quot;The Great Curse made her set up the Realm like that.&quot;<br /> <br /> People would rightfully say that was bullshit.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse is fine as a background element as long as it stays in the background - the Solars were slowly going crazy because of the Great Curse and Creation was doomed and the Great Prophecy said they were pretty much irredeemable without bringing a serious risk to Creation itself. Okay, cool.<br /> <br /> But the moment the Great Curse steps forward and starts being given credit for the specific events - &quot;Oh, the Sidereal chose the Bronze Prophecy because the Great Curse made them do it,&quot; is when the Great Curse stops being a narrative device and becomes a ham-fisted actor driving the game forward. And I do not think it's good for the gameline if the authors put the Great Curse in the driver's seat with both hands locked in a death-grip on the steering wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:15:10-07:00","id":971960,"title":"","content":"The great curse didn't make the siderials choose the bronze prophecy. It ensured that something would go wrong no matter what they picked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:25:32-07:00","id":971968,"title":"","content":"Again, saying that the Sidereal Exalted have never figured out that creatures outside of Fate exist, creatures who could mess up the Great Prophecy, doesn't make a lot sense when they spend time actively hunting down and killing those creatures and the only response we've gotten is, &quot;The Great Curse blinds them.&quot; <br /> <br /> Further, the game has said that the Great Curse makes the Sidereal arrogant and intractable and specifically noted that the Great Prophecy was among the most important events that was charted by the Great Curse. <br /> <br /> Having the Great Curse in the background is fine. Having it as an actor driving the events of a splat is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-18-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:49:42-07:00","id":972010,"title":"","content":"I'll have a punt again and maybe more broadly than having an impact on the Sidereals alone, rhetorically, I do feel there's a bit of a difference between<br /> <br /> &quot;You are the greatest, but cursed to extreme emotion and pride, and you were eventually overthrown as this led you to increasing injustices&quot; against<br /> <br /> &quot;You were cursed to think that you were able to make a competent decision about who should be in power over you, and so made a rebellion that was incompetent in conception and ruinous for everyone&quot;. Which leaning a lot on the Sidereal Great Curse, as it stands, for the Usurpation maybe can get close to.<br /> <br /> The second of these strikes more against what I think is maybe one of the important Exalted setting things (if we're still allowed to be this pretentious in the current age of Exalted fandom <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) where the setting is a bit pro or at least neutral to people judging their rulers and them being willing to tear them down if it means their own wellbeing and freedom over their destiny. Generally, players as Solars looking at the structure of the Age of Sorrows as it stands and rejecting it.<br /> <br /> Maybe like for a comparison if you shifted conflict of the returned Solars with the Realm into &quot;Well, they could make peace, and solve things without any death, destruction and revolution, without any tradeoffs, but they can't because of the Great Curse will stop them making that decision&quot;. It could seem a bit like undermining the idea of thinking about why people really take revolutionary and violent political activity against the powers that be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T02:05:17-07:00","id":972410,"title":"","content":"I will say that at least in 2e the Flawed Fates did not necessarily advocate UNWISE decisions. It drove the Sidereals to excesses of their Maidens' purviews.<br /> <br /> A Battles who limit breaks while guiding Romeo and Juliet forgets all about the whole 'doomed romance that makes the heads see their folly' thing and turns the cold war-style feud into outright war in the streets between the families of Montague and Capulet, which is SO INCREDIBLY BLOODY that both sides grow utterly sick of it and abandon the feud, burying the hatchet.<br /> <br /> She accomplishes her goal (end the feud), but does it in a Mars-y way that might not be the best way (after all, the families are decimated, as opposed to just two idiot teenagers offing themselves), but isn't 'pants-on-head-stupid'. Just, she can't NOT see red, so to speak. In this light...<br /> <br /> [85% of the Sidereals] *limit break simultaneously apparently if the Great Curse is what drove the Usurpation*<br /> [Journeys] If the world might end, all journeys and beginnings and everything would never happen. That's not good. *chooses the sure bet*<br /> [Serenity] If the world might end, all happiness and births and everything would never happen. That's not good. *chooses the sure bet*<br /> [Battles] If the world might end, all conflicts and struggles and strifes everything would never happen. That's not good. *chooses the sure bet*<br /> [Secrets] If the world might end, nothing would ever again be learned or concealed or understood. That's not good. *chooses the sure bet*<br /> [Endings] If the world might end, everything would end.... but then nothing would ever end again. That's not good. *chooses the sure bet*<br /> [15% of the Sidereals] So, do we want to try the uncertain long shot?<br /> [85%] No. Sure bet it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 09-19-2016, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T02:29:55-07:00","id":972417,"title":"","content":"I think Flawed Fate was a small step up from the Sidereals having no limit break because a lot of players and writers didn't know how to be subtle with hubris and it frequently ended up feeling like they were in constant limit break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:50:30-07:00","id":973187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=971968#post971968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having the Great Curse in the background is fine. Having it as an actor driving the events of a splat is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Curse isn't allowed in the driver's seat, who drove a busload of Solars off the bridge and into Lake Cray-Cray during the First Age?<br /> <br /> =====<br /> Frankly, the endless mewling about the Curse as regards the Prophecy and the Usurpation on these forums is one reason I cut the Curse entirely. Exalted to me is all shades of gray. It's tiresome and pointless to dissect where the Bronze Faction is just making a judgment call and where they are Cursed into hubris. The Solars of the First Age were a danger to Creation, but they might have been its salvation as well.<br /> <br /> I'm getting to the end of my story with my noobs. I started with five sheltered Realm Patricians, sent them into the Threshold, and thrashed them. I beat them over the head with the oppression and humiliation heaped on the satrapies. Then, I slowly peeled back the layers of deceit in the Immaculate Order. One PC (not one of the noobs) started with a defining Intimacy of belief in the Immaculate Texts, and ended up stabbing a Dynast in the back while she fought off a Lunar Anathema.<br /> <br /> Then they went home to their Tepet boss, and he laid it out for them. The Immaculate Order is a tool. They didn't need to believe, they just need to understand the utility. The simple truth is if the Lunars win, the PCs and all their friends and family will die. There's a war, and they are one side, and the &quot;Anathema&quot; are on the other. Any horrors they have seen in the Threshold keep the Realm in power, and they are no worse and no better than similar horrors perpetrated by the Lunars, or the Bull of the North.<br /> <br /> The look on their faces when they understood it comes down to who dies and who lives was priceless. And that's Exalted. No Curse required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:17:19-07:00","id":973210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=973187#post973187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Curse isn't allowed in the driver's seat, who drove a busload of Solars off the bridge and into Lake Cray-Cray during the First Age?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I ran my (admittedly singular) Exalted game. Probably the single quote that has stuck with me the entire time I have played Exalted is this:<br /> <br /> &quot; <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>And this, my friends, is what happens to Elder Solar Exalted.</i> <br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>The corruption of the Great Curse, the soul-rot that consumes all of them. The strongest, the brightest, the best and the noblest of them, it matters not. You live long enough, you turn from an exemplar of glorious perfection to one who perfectly embodies virtue corrupted.</i> <br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Conviction becomes careless cruelty and a cavalier attitude to ever-increasing amounts of collateral damage.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Valor becomes sneering contempt at reason.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Temperance teeters back and forth between mortification of the flesh, one's own and those of others, for failing to adhere to impossible standards, and to the wildest excesses a thousand screaming souls sing of in their unending nightmares.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Compassion devolves into brutal micromanagement of lives, no matter what these objects - objects! - of affection want, because you know better.</i> <br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>And then you add Limit Breaks, which exaggerate all these titanic flaws to levels previously unseen, unheard and unimagined, for centuries upon centuries.</i> <br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>There is no escape from this fate, for so rot-blighted are these ancient souls that not even death can end their evil. There is only the time your Exaltation gives you before the Great Curse consumes you, and in that time, you can be the hero you were meant to be.</i> <br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Just pray that you die long before one of your younger cousins stands before you, raging at you, casting words of fiery damnation at you for in your heart you will know that you have become the very monster your kind was made to fight. &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> </i>In my games, <u>all</u> of the Exalted steadily go insane. Not even through the actions of the Great Curse, but also through sheer separation from humanity. The best part was when the players went along with it, without truly realizing what was happening. They were <u>so sure</u> of their moral superiority, because they were <u>Exalted</u>, and they were fighting <u>The Realm</u>, how could they be wrong? It got to the point where every spear not aimed at the Realm was one aimed at them, every voice not raised in support was one grumbling in rebellion. Any village that didn't outright support them immediately was purged, because a lack of outright support indicated a lack of moral fibre, one that could be exploited by the Realm.<br /> <br /> The best part was: I didn't have to do all that much. They didn't even have all that many Limit Breaks. The descent into insanity was all them, them being <u>so sure</u> that what they were doing was right, that they would sacrifice as many mortal lives as they needed in order to win. I had one player actually say to me,&quot; The mortals live short, shitty lives, right? Why do they care how they die, they are just going to reincarnate anyways. Stopping the Realm is more important.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>That</i></u></b> was my Great Curse. When I laid it out for them at the end of the campaign, they had one of these moments.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hn1VxaMEjRU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hn1VxaMEjRU</a></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:34:46-07:00","id":973221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=973187#post973187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Curse isn't allowed in the driver's seat, who drove a busload of Solars off the bridge and into Lake Cray-Cray during the First Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, from a setting perspective there's a vast difference between the idea that the Solars suffered from a terrible and insidious curse that slowly made them mad and, if left unchecked, would have caused them to eventually threaten the existence of Creation, and the game stating that the Great Curse is why the Sidereal Exalted chose the Bronze Vision rather than the Gold Vision.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse as a dark idea that stays in the background as an ominous effect that occasionally causes problems in undefined ways is great. But when the game begins specifically drawing cause and effect relationships between the Great Curse and specific events it's a failure.<br /> <br /> Imagine if the gameline said something like, &quot;The Tepet Legion's attack against the Bull failed because the Great Curse caused the Dragon Blooded to be overconfident.&quot; That would be bullshit. There are lots of good reasons for why the Tepet Legion's attack on the Bull might have failed, but attributing the failure to the Great Curse would be putting too much emphasis on it in a way that is bad for the game.<br /> <br /> Basically there are good ways and bad ways to use the Great Curse, but when the gameline uses it as the specific cause for specific events, that is incredibly hamfisted and very bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-20-2016, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:30:36-07:00","id":973293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=970349#post970349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there some write up online where the vision of Gold lead to Solars mentally dominating Creation. They were the mad blood thirsty gods who did horrible things and you thanked them for it.<br /> <br /> I think Jena Moran wrote it up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're talking about <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zaraborgstrom/SolarMonsters\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:04:01-07:00","id":973326,"title":"","content":"Rereading Jena's old comments. I sure do miss her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">On what would happen if the Sidereals made everyone's life boring</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">rebeccaborgstrom - 11/03/2003 18:56:58</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I suspect that the shards would still find people to Exalt, even if everyone's life was entirely banal. The stories would be less exciting, though.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">**<br /> &quot;So I was a little short on cash, and couldn't afford to have ice cream with my meal.&quot;<br /> &quot;That's horrible, Jane.&quot;<br /> &quot;I know. But I just set my chin and said, 'Well, if I can't have ice cream, I'll just have to carry on with the roast beef sandwich.'&quot;<br /> &quot;Wow.&quot;<br /> &quot;But then the same thing happened *again* the next day!&quot;<br /> &quot;You poor thing.&quot;<br /> &quot;So I set my jaw again, and said, 'Maybe I don't *need* ice cream.' Even though my stomach was rumbling and my sweet tooth was aching!&quot;<br /> &quot;You are SO STRONG.&quot;<br /> &quot;Then the ice cream vendor looked up, and his eyes were full of moonlight. 'Jane Fitzsimmons,' he said, 'who labors to endure, in the face of such terrible hardship; I name you as my Chosen. And your totem shall be the great caribou, strength of the north.'&quot;<br /> &quot;What did you do?&quot;<br /> &quot;I said, 'Okay, but can I have some ice cream?' And he said, 'all the ice cream in the world is yours; you have only to seize it.'&quot;<br /> &quot;Wow.&quot;<br /> &quot;So I said, 'including this frozen Snickers ice cream bar?' And he nodded. So I took it. This Exaltation is, like, the best thing ever.&quot;<br /> &quot;Wow! He just let you take it?&quot;<br /> &quot;It was like, nobody can stop me now!&quot;</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I think that's still my favorite thing anyone has ever posted on the Exalted forums.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:13:06-07:00","id":973338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=973293#post973293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're talking about <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zaraborgstrom/SolarMonsters\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. That. <br /> <br /> I consider the end of the Solar First Age a &quot;damned if you do, damned if you don't situation&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:46:59-07:00","id":973926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=973221#post973221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, from a setting perspective there's a vast difference between the idea that the Solars suffered from a terrible and insidious curse that slowly made them mad and, if left unchecked, would have caused them to eventually threaten the existence of Creation, and the game stating that the Great Curse is why the Sidereal Exalted chose the Bronze Vision rather than the Gold Vision.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse as a dark idea that stays in the background as an ominous effect that occasionally causes problems in undefined ways is great. But when the game begins specifically drawing cause and effect relationships between the Great Curse and specific events it's a failure.<br /> <br /> Imagine if the gameline said something like, &quot;The Tepet Legion's attack against the Bull failed because the Great Curse caused the Dragon Blooded to be overconfident.&quot; That would be bullshit. There are lots of good reasons for why the Tepet Legion's attack on the Bull might have failed, but attributing the failure to the Great Curse would be putting too much emphasis on it in a way that is bad for the game.<br /> <br /> Basically there are good ways and bad ways to use the Great Curse, but when the gameline uses it as the specific cause for specific events, that is incredibly hamfisted and very bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, you're slicing that mighty thin.<br /> <br /> Saying the Great Curse is the reason the Sids went Bronze is bad.<br /> Saying the Great Curse is the reason the Solars went bad is good.<br /> <br /> Both of the above involve choices. Both of the above involve fateful decisions with irreparable consequences for Creation. The Solars weren't going mad. They were already Jared Leto in make-up, and their war was going to end the world as everyone knew it. The Curse isn't some implied cause, here. The Solars going nuts is Exhibit A for the power and danger of the Curse in the first place. So, essentially, you want a world where the Curse grabs the steering wheel long enough to drive the Solars off the cliff, then sits back and chills.<br /> <br /> Which I suppose is fine. The game can't exist without the Usurpation, and the devs have been worshipping at the altar of the Curse, so it's gotta be in there. Just don't pretend there's unity of presentation, here. The Curse is Deus Ex Machina, and the curtain is pretty thin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:22:07-07:00","id":973936,"title":"","content":"Again, it's the difference in presentation, between keeping something as a background detail and instead choosing to shine a spotlight on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Solars went crazy and did things.&quot; Okay, what kind of things? Who knows. They don't really matter during the 2nd Age and the actual details of what the Solars did are kind of irrelevant at this point in time. All that matters is that the Great Curse was insidious and subtly pushing the Solars to become BBEGs who threatened to destroy the world. And it's important to remember that the Solars weren't necessarily BBEG's at that time. Just that the Prophecy showed that they all <i>would</i> become BBEGs in the future, and destroy Creation unless they were &quot;dealt with.&quot;<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Sidereal Exalted's decision to choose the Bronze Vision over the Gold Vision is incredibly important to the current setting of the gameline (it's a major plot point for Sidereal PC's), and for the game to say that decision was the result of the Great Curse puts the Great Curse in the spotlight on the Great Curse way that's bad for the game. <br /> <br /> This isn't only true of the Great Curse but many other facets of the game as well. Some things are okay if they're left in the background and not really explored very much. It's fine to make a note that mortals in Malfeas face terrible abuse at the hands of demons there, and perhaps make dry listing of some of the terrible fates that await them. But it's completely different when the gameline begins giving that specific focus, detailing at length the abuses that a specific human in Malfeas (Lilun) faces.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Great Curse as a background detail and character flaw is acceptable, and it's acceptable as a vague excuse for why &quot;sometimes bad stuff happened,&quot; but the moment the gameline begins using it as a &quot;cause and effect&quot; reason for why <i>specific</i> events unfolded in the way that they did, that's where it's an issue and being used in a hamfisted manner - especially for something like the Gold vs Bronze prophecy, which is supposed to have some feeling of nuance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:29:32-07:00","id":973943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=973926#post973926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying the Great Curse is the reason the Sids went Bronze is bad.<br /> Saying the Great Curse is the reason the Solars went bad is good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, despite their similar phrasing these two concepts are actually <i>very </i>different beasts.<br /> <br /> Following the prophecy of bronze was one very specific decision. That's not how the Great Curse works. It didn't deliberately steer the solars to particular atrocities, it just sent them mad and let them express that madness however they wished. It's a state of being, not a driving force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:35:34-07:00","id":973946,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there is a way to use Arcane Fate/Broken Mask to take the spotlight off the Great Curse's part in the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> All the Sidereals who survived the Usurpation wake up in the Loom of Fate with no recollection of what has happened over the past year. They go about their day and realize two things: one, the Dragonblooded overthrew the Solars and two, no one remembers anything about who they are and what Sidereals are. The Sidereals look up in the sky and see the remains of the Broken Mask and figure they did something. While the Sidereals and rest of the Bureau of Destiny know who they are, no one can account for the Sidereals activities over the past year. After years of divine audits and hearings, the only charge the courts can make stick is &quot;Destroying Evidence.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Assumption is that Sidereals decided to get involved in the Usurpation (not sure if they recruited the Dragonblooded or the Dragonblooded recruited them). To cover up their involvement, they casts some major Astrology that went bad and left them with Arcane Fate. If a Great Prophecy was cast, no one remembers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:26:39-07:00","id":973970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=973943#post973943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, despite their similar phrasing these two concepts are actually <i>very </i>different beasts.<br /> <br /> Following the prophecy of bronze was one very specific decision. That's not how the Great Curse works. It didn't deliberately steer the solars to particular atrocities, it just sent them mad and let them express that madness however they wished. It's a state of being, not a driving force.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> One thing DotFA did really right was the Hierophant's relationship with the Great Curse Heart of Tears didn't make him commit atrocities but he recognised that other people suffering made him depressed so he stopped putting himself in situations where he was likely to encounter it and thus becomes blind to the atrocities of his peers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:25:13-07:00","id":974031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/966918-mental-stability-of-newly-exalted-solars?p=973926#post973926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, you're slicing that mighty thin.<br /> <br /> Saying the Great Curse is the reason the Sids went Bronze is bad.<br /> Saying the Great Curse is the reason the Solars went bad is good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's bad if taken as a strong reason, if it's functionally as a bait and switch from what we know about the Usurpation, and bad with the Sidereal Curse in its current form (hubris).<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be so bad if all we knew from the very start of the game was &quot;The Curse ate away at the hearts of the Exalted, leading them to passions, folly and war, and the Solars, the greatest, were ultimately the most diminished, and cast asunder&quot;. That would be &quot;Unity of presentation&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the Great Prophecy had never been set up as a resonant choice, and the Usurpation never as a struggle against tyranny. (I'd probably be like 75% okay with that as an alternative thing.)<br /> <br /> But if we're in the position of the setting is taking the choice of the Great Prophecy as a choice between a more glorious or a safer world seriously, then yes, it is bad to undermine that by bait and switch making the choice of the Paths of Bronze and Golds due to the Great Curse. Even if &quot;unity of presentation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}